  <section>
    <h2>Dispensaries in Ellsworth</h2>

    <h3>Curaleaf Maine — Ellsworth</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 180 High St, Ellsworth, ME 04605<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 664-0008<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> Mon-Sat 10am-7pm, Sun 11am-5pm<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical-only (MMMP cardholders)</p>
    <p>Curaleaf's Ellsworth location is one of the company's multi-state medical dispensaries, serving Hancock County's registered patients. The brand's scale brings consistent product availability, with standardized strains, vape cartridges, and edibles carried across all of its Maine locations. Ellsworth's Curaleaf is the closest Curaleaf to Acadia for medical visitors who want a familiar national brand.</p>

    <h3>Maine Organic Therapy — Ellsworth</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 147 State St, Ellsworth, ME 04605<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 667-4400<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> Mon-Sat 10am-6pm<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical (MMMP) with adult-use product line</p>
    <p>Maine Organic Therapy (MOT) operates a medical dispensary in Ellsworth and is widely recognized as one of Maine's longest-running caregiver networks. Their Ellsworth storefront offers flower, concentrates, tinctures, and topicals, and they have a strong reputation with patients seeking organically grown, terpene-forward products.</p>

    <h3>Main Street Medical — Ellsworth</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 199 Main St, Ellsworth, ME 04605<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 610-1100<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> Mon-Fri 10am-6pm, Sat 10am-4pm<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical (MMMP) with adult-use options</p>
    <p>Main Street Medical serves Ellsworth's medical patient base with an adult-use component as well. Located on the downtown Main Street corridor, the dispensary is well-positioned for both local patients and travelers from the Bar Harbor / Acadia region making the 25-mile trip down US-1.</p>
  </section>

  <Callout title="Acadia Gateway" type="passion">
    Ellsworth sits at the intersection of US-1 and ME-3, the two routes that funnel almost all Acadia NP visitors into Bar Harbor. For dispensary operators, this creates a built-in tourism channel: an Ellsworth dispensary can capture both Hancock County patients and the steady stream of summer visitors who arrive via I-395 and exit at Ellsworth's commercial strip.
  </Callout>

  <section>
    <h2>Ellsworth's Market Context</h2>
    <p>Ellsworth is the largest town in Downeast Maine and the regional commercial hub for Hancock County. The town has historically anchored retail, healthcare, and government services for a wide swath of the eastern coast, and cannabis is no exception: with three or more dispensaries operating in town, Ellsworth is functionally the cannabis gateway to Acadia NP — the most-visited national park in the northeastern United States.</p>
    <p>Acadia draws roughly 4 million visitors per year, with peak summer traffic flowing through Ellsworth on ME-3 toward Bar Harbor and Mount Desert Island. The town also benefits from year-round residents across the broader Downeast region — including Machias, Blue Hill, Deer Isle, and the Blue Hill Peninsula — for whom Ellsworth is the nearest full-service dispensary cluster.</p>
    <p>Operators evaluating Downeast Maine should treat Ellsworth as the anchor market: medical-only MSOs (Curaleaf), caregiver networks (Maine Organic Therapy), and combined medical/adult-use storefronts (Main Street Medical) have all validated demand, and the town's role as a service hub for the surrounding rural region gives it a stable year-round patient base that recreational-only operators in tourist towns may not have.</p>
  </section>

